# NFL source registry - GENERATED by scripts/build_registry.py
#
# Regenerating replaces the `sources` list and preserves `profile`.
#
# URLs come from two verified patterns (SB Nation /rss/index.xml and
# MLB.com /feeds/news/rss.xml), NOT from a live check of each one. Feeds rot.
# Before trusting any of this:
#
#   python -m beatwire.cli doctor --sport nfl
#   python -m beatwire.cli verify --sport nfl --fix
#
# The disabled `-local` entries are the hand-research slots: one local daily
# or beat podcast per team. Filling those in is the single highest-value
# manual task in this project, and the one worth paying someone to do.

profile:
  display: NFL
  positions:
  - QB
  - RB
  - WR
  - TE
  - K
  - DEF
  - OL
  - DL
  - LB
  - CB
  - S
  high_value:
  - practice participation changes (DNP, limited, full)
  - first-team reps at a skill position
  - backfield or slot role changes
  - a starter ruled in or out
  - injury designations and return timelines
  low_value:
  - generic optimism from a coach about a player working hard
  - offseason workout program attendance
  - contract restructures with no roster impact
  notes: 'NFL practices are largely closed to the public, so the beat writer in the building is frequently
    the only source in the world for a given fact. Camp and Wednesday through Friday practice reports
    carry the most signal. Coachspeak is abundant and mostly worthless; prefer observed reps over quoted
    praise.

    '
sources:
